Build the initial MVP for "Harmony Acres" — an AI-enabled farm delivery subscription 
platform. This build covers the backend API and the conversational agent layer only. 
No frontend.

## Hard Rules

    Build this one section at at a time. Imagine you are a senior Software engineer skilled in AI and agent integration. Imagine I am a more junior engineer trying to understand these systems. Explain to me every step you take, the logic behind it, and the tradeoffs behind the decision. Use the Amazon Bedrock API to use whatever agents you need.
## Stack
- Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.11+)
- Database: PostgreSQL via Neon — use the pooled connection string (the `-pooler`
  endpoint, which multiplexes connections through PgBouncer in transaction mode) since
  this will later run in serverless/short-lived-connection environments. Use SQLAlchemy
  (async, via asyncpg) as the ORM.
- Agent: Strands Agents SDK, using strands.models.BedrockModel as the model provider
  (Amazon Bedrock, not restricted to bare Converse calls — leverage BedrockModel's
  support for inference profiles and Guardrails hooks, since we'll wire in a Guardrail
  later).
- Auth: JWT-based, custom (not a hosted auth provider) — role separation between
  "customer" and "admin".

