## README.md

Cover: prerequisites (Python version, Neon project setup, AWS credentials for
Bedrock), how to run migrations, how to run the seed script, how to start the FastAPI
server, how to run the agent's terminal loop separately, and a short "known limitations" 
section noting this MVP has no frontend, no Guardrails yet, and agent/API share a process 
rather than talking over Gateway/HTTP (that comes when we move to AgentCore).

Build this in dependency order: DB models + migrations first, then services, then
routers, then seed script, then agent tools, then agent entrypoint. Confirm each layer
runs before moving to the next.